    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 73c88116a5aa6ce171e772310e3eaa74e9c1d623 -->\n**Ready for the maintainer to merge.** Full review of head 73c88116, trial-merged with current main (clean, no conflicts).\n\n**What looks good**\n- The merge c81ade49 holds up under `git show --remerge-diff`. In `types/mod.rs` the export line keeps main's `sinker` re-export and this PR's `DEFAULT_CLEARANCE`. In `wire_post.rs`, `GOLDEN` is main's `wire_slug_punch.nc`, `OPEN_GOLDEN` is added, and both main's #1139/#1144 tests and the new open-cutoff test survive. Nothing from main was dropped.\n- Main's wire verify law judges the new moves. `wire_verify.rs:93` maps `left|right` to `CutSide::Open`, so the kerf/gouge law covers the run-in, run and run-out. The start-hole and slug laws are skipped on purpose and the report says so. `wire_post::an_open_cutoff_posts_its_golden_and_a_gouging_one_is_refused` posts the open golden and refuses the gouging variant with no NC written. The slug punch golden is asserted unchanged.\n- Refusals are named, `side` has no serde default, and the closed path is byte-identical.\n- No new unwrap/expect/panic in the new code. New files are under 400 lines (`open.rs` 355). There is a provenance line and a decision file (`docs/decisions/1109-wire-open-profile.md`). No Cargo.toml or build.rs change, no process files, no snapshot PNGs.\n- The PR carries only its own 7 commits over main (#1144 and its parents are already merged).\n\n**Local results (merged with main)**\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| motion lib | 228 passed, 4 ignored |\n| sim lib | 119 passed |\n| post `script_wire_iso` | 11 passed |\n| app lib | 160 passed |\n| app wire_contour / wire_post / wire_readers / wire_verify / mcp_wire_contour | 8 / 8 / 7 / 3 / 4 passed |\n| app golden_cl / solid_law_goldens (posted_gates) / feature_pick_wire / edm_machine / edm_conditions | 27 / 6 / 4 / 5 / 1 passed |\n| ui lib | 641 passed, 5 ignored |\n| clippy motion, sim, app, ui `--all-targets -D warnings` | clean |\n\n**Requested before merge**: none.\n\n**Notes (not blocking)**\n- `wire_page.rs` gains side options and a \"Run-out clearance\" row, and the PR body has no before/after screenshot. This is a note only; the UI test lib is green.\n- Not exercised on a real EDM control; the condition and EDM codes are synthetic, as the body says.\n- Effort is high, which fits the safety floor.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
